int binarySearch(const vector<int>& arr, int target) {
    int lo = 0, hi = arr.size() - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
        int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == target) return mid;
        if (arr[mid] < target) lo = mid + 1;
        else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return -1;
}
```

`lo + (hi - lo) / 2` avoids overflow that `(lo + hi) / 2` can hit on large indices. The loop narrows the range by half each pass and returns the index, or -1 if the target isn't present.

Time O(log n), space O(1).
